Not as bad as you expect; with higher enchantments magicbane loses
more and more of it's magical attack properties, you exchanged that for
a bit more damage done.

> 2. Soon after I found that problem, I got a Frost Brand from
> sacrificing.  Should I switch to Frost Brand, or should I stay with my
> +4 Magicbane?  I found there are a lot of debates over best Wizard
> weapon here.

The damage from Magicbane (ignoring the magic attacks) at expert
proficiency is worse than basic longsword damage; and Frostbrand
will do additional damage from it's cold attack.

If you can ascend that character Magicbane will be your weapon for
the homerun because it absorbs the random curses.

But the primary way for a wizard to attack are his spells. Because of
his high maximum dagger skill it's also good to throw daggers.

> 3. I do not find a lot scroll of enchant armor along the way, so my AC
> is still -1.  While that seems enough for me now, I am afraid I can be
> easily taken out with one or two strikes by stronger monsters. 

Yes, that's right. A mumakil or a minotaur (or a swarm of soldier ants)
will easily kill you. So don't rely on your armor, have an escape route
whereever you are, do your planning in advance. Try to look for better
armor; Fort Knox, The Castle, and Zoos may have dragon that provide
you some material for a dragon armor.

